{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["And you shall make a tzitz — because it is placed on the forehead, the place where people see, it is called ציץ, as in ״מציץ מן החרכים״; as I explained regarding המשקוף, so it appears to me." "קדש לה׳ — on the ephod and on the breastpiece were the names of the children of Israel for a remembrance, for the Holy One, blessed be He, made atonement for the sin of consecrated things that the children of Israel whose names were inscribed below might consecrate — through the tzitz, by means of the stones of the ephod and the breastpiece. קדש לה׳ — that is, the Holy One, blessed be He, propitiates the sin of consecrated things."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:29.652222948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}